      en: "Areng Valley, deep in the Cardamom Mountains, is a pristine wilderness harboring one of Southeast Asia's largest remaining elephant populations (around 150 individuals). Its primary rainforest features trees over 40 meters tall and a dense understory of palms and ferns. Indigenous communities maintain traditional livelihoods, including rice cultivation and non-timber forest product collection. The Areng River cascades down a 20-meter waterfall, creating a vital water source for wildlife. Conservation efforts have limited development, preserving the valley's ecological integrity.",
